67d|v|To prepare, as food, by cooking in a dry heat, either in an oven or under coals, or on heated stone or metal; as, to bake bread, meat, apples. ; To dry or harden (anything) by subjecting to heat, as, to bake bricks; the sun bakes the ground. ; To harden by cold. ; To do the work of baking something; as, she brews, washes, and bakes. ; To be baked; to become dry and hard in heat; as, the bread bakes; the ground bakes in the hot sun.	o:fw9,130,3~fw9,130,3	d:23hz,36,4~23hz,36,4
