6jp|n|A carpentry obstruction, stockade, or other obstacle made in a passage in order to stop an enemy. ; A fortress or fortified town, on the frontier of a country, commanding an avenue of approach. ; A fence or railing to mark the limits of a place, or to keep back a crowd. ; An any obstruction; anything which hinders approach or attack. ; Any limit or boundary; a line of separation.	a:23ln,88,20~23ln,88,20	n:161p,74,7;xuk,51,6~161p,74,7;xuk,51,6	N:25yc,85,3;25xr,65,6;26cl,59,6~26cl,59,6;25xr,65,6;25yc,85,3
6jp|v|A carpentry obstruction, stockade, or other obstacle made in a passage in order to stop an enemy. ; A fortress or fortified town, on the frontier of a country, commanding an avenue of approach. ; A fence or railing to mark the limits of a place, or to keep back a crowd. ; An any obstruction; anything which hinders approach or attack. ; Any limit or boundary; a line of separation.	d:xuk,25,1~xuk,25,1
